          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            A
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differentiable+manifold"} differentiable manifold
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topological space
            which is
            %em locally
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homeomorphism"} homeomorphic
            to a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Euclidean+space"} Euclidean space
            (a
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+manifold"} topological manifold
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gluing+functions"} gluing functions
            which relate these Euclidean
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/local+charts"} local charts
            to each other are
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differentiable+functions"} differentiable functions
            = succeed "." do
              %em smooth manifolds
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/manifold"} manifold
          %p
            Differential and smooth manifolds are the basis for much of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+geometry"} differential geometry
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/schemes"} schemes
            are in
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebraic+geometry"} algebraic geometry
          %p
            If one relaxes the condition from being locally isomorphic to a Euclidean space to admitting local smooth maps from a Euclidean space, then one obtains the concept of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diffeological+spaces"} diffeological spaces
            or even
            = succeed ";" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+sets"} smooth sets
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generalized+smooth+space"} generalized smooth space
            for more on this.
          %p
            The generalization of differentiable manifolds to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+differential+geometry"} higher differential geometry
            are
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orbifolds"} orbifolds
            and more generally
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differentiable+stacks"} differentiable stacks
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+sets"} smooth sets
            then one obtains the concept of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+stacks"} smooth stacks
            and eventually
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+infinity-stacks"} smooth infinity-stacks
          %p
            Smooth manifolds form a category,
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/SmoothManifolds"} SmoothManifolds
          %h2#definition Definition
          %h3#traditional_definition Traditional definition
          %p
            For the traditional definition, see at
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differentiable+manifold"} differentiable manifold
          %h3#patching_as_idempotent_splitting Patching as idempotent splitting
          %p
            The lecture notes
            %a{:href => "#Lawvere73"} Lawvere 1973, Ex. 3.21
            reported a somewhat surprising observation:
          %p
            In the case of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+manifolds"} smooth manifolds
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Karoubi+envelope"} splitting of idempotents
            in a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+open+subsets"} category of open subsets
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Euclidean+spaces"} Euclidean spaces
          %p
            Let
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Diff"}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Diff
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Diff
            be the category of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+manifolds"} smooth manifolds
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+maps"} smooth maps
            = succeed "-" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+number"} finite
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dimension+of+a+manifold"} dimensional
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/second-countable+topological+space"} second-countable
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hausdorff+space"} Hausdorff
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+manifold"}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^\infty
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/manifold"} manifold
            without
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/boundary+of+a+manifold"} boundary
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi i
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi Open
                  %mo ↪
                  %mi Diff
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i \colon Open \hookrightarrow Diff
            be the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/full+subcategory"} full subcategory
            whose objects are the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/open+subspaces"} open subspaces
            of
            = succeed "-" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+number"} finite
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dimension+of+a+manifold"} dimensional
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cartesian+spaces"} Cartesian spaces
          %p
          #IdSplittingCompletionTheorem.num_theorem
            %h6 Theorem
            %p
            %p
              The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subcategory"} subcategory
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi i
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi Open
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi Diff
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i \colon Open \hookrightarrow Diff
              exhibits
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Diff
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Diff
              as an idempotent-splitting completion of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Open
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Open
            %p
          .proof
            %h6#proof Proof
            %p
              By a general
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Karoubi+envelope#def2"} lemma for idempotent splittings
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  every smooth manifold is a smooth
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/retract"} retract
                  of an open set in Euclidean space; and
              %li
                %p
                  if
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi p
                        %mo :
                        %mi U
                        %mo →
                        %mi U
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p : U \to U
                  is a smooth idempotent on an open set
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi U
                          %mo ⊆
                          %msup
                            %mi ℝ
                            %mi n
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U \subseteq \mathbb{R}^n
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi Fix
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi p
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ↪
                        %mi U
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Fix(p) \hookrightarrow U
                  is an
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/embedding+of+smooth+manifolds"} embedded
                  submanifold.
            %p
              For the first statement, we use the fact that any manifold
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi M
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
              can be realized as a closed submanifold of some
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi ℝ
                        %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^n
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tubular+neighborhood+theorem"} tubular neighborhood
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi U
                      %mo ⊆
                      %msup
                        %mi ℝ
                        %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U \subseteq \mathbb{R}^n
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
              carries the structure of a vector bundle over
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi M
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
              in such a way that the inclusion
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi M
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi U
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M \hookrightarrow U
              is identified with the zero section, so that the bundle projection
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                    %mo →
                    %mi M
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U \to M
              provides a retraction, with right inverse given by the zero section.
            %p
              For the second statement (cf.
              = succeed ")," do
                %a{:href => "#Zack14"} Zack 2014
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0
              is a fixed point of
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi p
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi T
                      %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≅
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T_0(U) \cong \mathbb{R}^n
              be its tangent space (observe the presence of a
              %em canonical
              isomorphism to
              = succeed ")." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi ℝ
                        %mi n
