                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+stack"} smooth stack
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+infinity-stack"} smooth infinity-stack
            %li
              %p
                %a{:href => "cohesive+%28infinity%2C1%29-topos+--+infinitesimal+cohesion#CohesivemanifoldsSeparated"} differential cohesion – structures - Cohesive manifolds (separated)
          %h2#references References
          %blockquote
            %p
              (see also the references at
              = succeed ")" do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+geometry"} differential geometry
          %p
            The vision of the modern notion of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/manifolds"} manifolds
            is attributed to:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bernhard+Riemann"}> Bernhard Riemann
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%C3%9Cber+die+Hypothesen%2C+welche+der+Geometrie+zu+Grunde+liegen"} Über die Hypothesen, welche der Geometrie zu Grunde liegen
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-642-35121-1"} doi:10.1007/978-3-642-35121-1
              %p
                Engl. transl:
                = succeed ":" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/William+Clifford"} William Clifford
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/On+the+hypotheses+which+underlie+geometry"} On the hypotheses which underlie geometry
                %strong VIII
                (1873) 183-184 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-319-26042-6"}> doi:10.1007/978-3-319-26042-6
                \&amp;rbrack;
          %p Further historical contributions:
          %ul
            %li#VeblenWhitehead1931
              %p
                Oswald Veblen and
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/J.H.C.+Whitehead"} J.H.C. Whitehead
                = succeed "," do
                  %em A set of axioms for differential geometry
            %li#VeblenWhitehead1932
              %p
                Oswald Veblen and
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/J.H.C.+Whitehead"} J.H.C. Whitehead
                = succeed "," do
                  %em The foundations of differential geometry
            %li#Whitney1936
              %p
                Hassler
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Whitney"} Whitney
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Differentiable manifolds
          %p
            Early account with an eye towards
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cobordism+theory"} cobordism theory
            and the
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Pontrjagin-Thom+isomorphism"} Pontrjagin-Thom isomorphism
          %ul
            %li#Pontrjagin55
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lev+Pontrjagin"}> Lev Pontrjagin
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Smooth manifolds and their applications in Homotopy theory
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "https://web.math.rochester.edu/people/faculty/doug/otherpapers/pont4.pdf"} pdf
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://www.worldscientific.com/doi/abs/10.1142/9789812772107_0001"} doi:10.1142/9789812772107_0001
          %p Textbook accounts:
          %ul
            %li#MilnorStasheff74
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/John+Milnor"}> John Milnor
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/James+Stasheff"} James Stasheff
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Characteristic Classes
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://press.princeton.edu/books/paperback/9780691081229/characteristic-classes-am-76-volume-76"} ISBN:9780691081229
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Frank+W.+Warner"}> Frank W. Warner
                \:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Foundations of Differentiable Manifolds and Lie Groups
                %strong 94
                (1983) &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/978-1-4757-1799-0"}> doi:10.1007/978-1-4757-1799-0
                \&amp;rbrack;
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Georges+de+Rham"}> Georges de Rham
                , Chapter I of:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Differentiable Manifolds – Forms, Currents, Harmonic Forms
                = succeed "," do
                  %strong 266
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-642-61752-2"} doi:10.1007/978-3-642-61752-2
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yvonne+Choquet-Bruhat"}> Yvonne Choquet-Bruhat
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/C%C3%A9cile+DeWitt-Morette"} Cécile DeWitt-Morette
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Analysis, manifolds and physics
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://www.elsevier.com/books/analysis-manifolds-and-physics-revised-edition/choquet-bruhat/978-0-444-86017-0"} ISBN:9780444860170
              %blockquote
                %p
                  (with an eye towards
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mathematical+physics"} mathematical physics
            %li#Bredon93
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Glen+Bredon"}> Glen Bredon
                , Chapter II of:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Topology and Geometry
                = succeed "," do
                  %strong 139
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://link.springer.com/book/10.1007/978-1-4757-6848-0"} doi:10.1007/978-1-4757-6848-0
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "http://virtualmath1.stanford.edu/~ralph/math215b/Bredon.pdf"} pdf
            %li#KolarSlovakMichor93
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ivan+Kolar"}> Ivan Kolar
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jan+Slovak"} Jan Slovak
                = succeed ":" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Peter+Michor"} Peter Michor
                %em Natural operations in differential geometry
                (1993, 1999) &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "http://www.emis.de/monographs/KSM/"}> web
                \&amp;rbrack;
            %li#Kosinski93
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Antoni+Kosinski"}> Antoni Kosinski
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Differential manifolds
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.maths.ed.ac.uk/~v1ranick/papers/kosinski.pdf"} pdf
            %li#Lee09
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jeffrey+Lee"}> Jeffrey Lee
                \:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Manifolds and differential geometry
                %strong 107
                (2009) &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://bookstore.ams.org/gsm-107"}> ISBN: 978-0-8218-4815-9
                ,
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1090/gsm/107"} doi:10.1090/gsm/107
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Helmut+Eschrig"}> Helmut Eschrig
                , section 3 of:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Topology and Geometry for Physics
                = succeed "]" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-642-14700-5"} doi:10.1007/978-3-642-14700-5
            %li#Lee12
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/John+Lee"}> John Lee
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Introduction to Smooth Manifolds
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/978-1-4419-9982-5"} doi:10.1007/978-1-4419-9982-5
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://sites.math.washington.edu/~lee/Books/ISM/"} book webpage
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://math.berkeley.edu/~jchaidez/materials/reu/lee_smooth_manifolds.pdf"} pdf
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Theodore+Frankel"}> Theodore Frankel
                , chapter 1 of:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/The+Geometry+of+Physics+-+An+Introduction"} The Geometry of Physics - An Introduction
            %li#Nestruev02
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jet+Nestruev"}> Jet Nestruev
                \:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Smooth manifolds and Observables
                %strong 220
                Springer (2002, 2020) &amp;lbrack;ISBN:0-387-95543-7,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-030-45650-4"} doi:10.1007/978-3-030-45650-4
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://diffiety.mccme.ru/books/nestrspr.htm"} book webpage
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://nzdr.ru/data/media/biblio/kolxoz/M/MD/MDdg/Nestruev%20J.%20Smooth%20Manifolds%20and%20Observables%20(ISBN%200387955437)(Springer,%202003)(224s)_MDdg_.pdf"} pdf
          %p
            With an eye towards application in
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mathematical+physics"} mathematical physics
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mikio+Nakahara"}> Mikio Nakahara
              , Chapter 3 of
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Geometry%2C+Topology+and+Physics"} Geometry, Topology and Physics
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1201/9781315275826"} doi:10.1201/9781315275826
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://alpha.sinp.msu.ru/~panov/LibBooks/GRAV/(Graduate_Student_Series_in_Physics)Mikio_Nakahara-Geometry,_Topology_and_Physics,_Second_Edition_(Graduate_Student_Series_in_Physics)-Institute_of_Physics_Publishing(2003).pdf"} pdf
          %p Smooth manifolds are defined as locally ringed spaces in
          %ul
            %li
              Juan A. Navarro González, and Juan B. Sancho de Salas,
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi C
                          %mn ∞
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^\infty
                  \-Differentiable Spaces
              %strong 1824
              2003.
          %p Discussion of smooth manifolds as colimits of the Cech nerves of their good open covers is also at
          %ul
            %li
              MathOverflow,
              %em
                %a{:href => "http://mathoverflow.net/questions/65684/gluing-of-manifolds-and-the-hausdorff-condition"} Gluing of manifolds and the Hausdorff condition
          %p
            The general abstract framework of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+geometry"} higher geometry
            referred to above is discussed in
          %ul
            %li#StrSp
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jacob+Lurie"}> Jacob Lurie
              ,
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Structured+Spaces"} Structured Spaces
          %p
            The proof of Thm.
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#IdSplittingCompletionTheorem"}
            above makes use of the observation in
          %ul
            %li#Zack14
              %a{:href => "http://mathoverflow.net/users/300/zack"}> Zack
              ,
              %em Idempotents split in category of smooth manifolds?
              (2014) &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "http://mathoverflow.net/q/162556"}> MO:q/162556
              \&amp;rbrack;
          %p and provides a solution to exercise 3.21 in:
          %ul
            %li#Lawvere73
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/William+Lawvere"}> William Lawvere
              ,
              %em Perugia Notes - Theory of Categories over a Base Topos
              , Ms. Università di Perugia 1973 &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://github.com/mattearnshaw/lawvere/blob/master/pdfs/1972-perugia-lecture-notes.pdf"}> pdf
              ,
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/LawverePerugia1972.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
          %p
            The
            %a{:href => "#LawvereComment"} above comment
            by Lawvere is taken from
          %ul
            %li#Law89
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/F.+William+Lawvere"}> F. William Lawvere
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Qualitative distinctions between some toposes of generalized graphs
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://conceptualmathematics.files.wordpress.com/2013/01/toposesofgeneralizedgraphs.pdf"} pdf
